1. **A clip-on microphone assembly, comprising:**  
a housing including a clip configured to removably attach the housing to a user or an article worn by the user;  
at least three spatially separated microphones supported by the housing and configured to generate respective microphone signals in response to incident acoustic energy;  
an accelerometer configured to generate acceleration data indicative of an orientation of the housing;  
one or more processors; and  
memory storing instructions that, when executed by the one or more processors, cause the one or more processors to:  
determine, from relative differences among the respective microphone signals, a direction of arrival of an acoustic source relative to the housing;  
determine the orientation of the housing based at least in part on the acceleration data;  
select a beam-steering direction based on both the determined direction of arrival and the determined orientation of the housing; and  
apply respective beamforming parameters to the microphone signals according to the selected beam-steering direction to generate an orientation-compensated output audio signal emphasizing sound received from the acoustic source.
